[{"text": "The assembly will now listen to a", "start": 4.56, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "statement delivered by his excellency", "start": 7.52, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Dr. Mustafa Kamal Madbulli, Prime", "start": 10.08, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "Minister of the Arab Republic of Egypt.", "start": 12.8, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort his", "start": 17.68, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "excellency and invite him to address the", "start": 19.92, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 22.0, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "In the name of God, the merciful, the", "start": 36.8, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "compassionate. Mr. Khalil Rahman,", "start": 38.399, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "President of the 81st session of the", "start": 40.64, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "United Nations General Assembly. Mr.", "start": 42.8, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "Antonio Guterish, Secretary General of", "start": 46.0, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "the United Nations. Your majesties,", "start": 48.239, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "excellencies, and highnesses, heads of", "start": 50.879, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "state and government, ladies and", "start": 53.199, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "gentlemen. At the outset, I am pleased", "start": 54.96, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "to extend my sincere congratulations to", "start": 58.0, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "his excellency Minister Khalil Rahman on", "start": 60.96, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "assuming the presidency of the current", "start": 63.52, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "session of the General Assembly. We", "start": 65.439, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "assure him of our full support and", "start": 67.76, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "confidence in his ability to", "start": 69.84, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "successfully steer the work of the", "start": 71.68, "duration": 3.439}, {"text": "session.", "start": 73.52, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "This year, the General Assembly convenes", "start": 75.119, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "under a theme that accurately reflects", "start": 77.759, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "the challenge facing the international", "start": 80.4, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "system, restoring trust and managing", "start": 82.64, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "transformation.", "start": 85.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "Our world is changing at a pace far", "start": 87.36, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "exceeding the ability of international", "start": 90.0, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "governance institutions to respond. Our", "start": 92.799, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "crisis does not lie in the absence of", "start": 95.759, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "charters and principles, but rather in", "start": 98.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "the widening gap between what we", "start": 100.64, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "proclaim and what we implement and", "start": 102.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "between those who make decisions and", "start": 105.119, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "those who are affected by them. Our", "start": 107.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "world does not need a merely symbolic", "start": 110.0, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "multilateralism that brings together", "start": 112.24, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "states in open discussions. Rather, it", "start": 115.119, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "needs effective multilateralism in which", "start": 117.759, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "every state has a voice and every people", "start": 120.159, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "receive a fair share of decisions,", "start": 123.04, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "opportunities, and resources. It is no", "start": 125.52, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "exaggeration to say that confidence in", "start": 128.479, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "the effectiveness of collective action", "start": 130.8, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "and the multilateral system has", "start": 132.879, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "declined. There is an urgent need to", "start": 134.8, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "restore adherence to international law", "start": 137.2, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "to avoid policies based on power", "start": 139.76, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "polarization and double standards. It is", "start": 142.239, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "no coincidence that the countries of the", "start": 145.68, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "global south which comprise the", "start": 147.76, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "overwhelming majority of the world's", "start": 150.0, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "population are among those most harmed", "start": 152.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "by the decline of the rule of", "start": 154.959, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "international law, the weakening role of", "start": 156.72, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "international organizations and the", "start": 159.44, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "fragility of global governance and", "start": 161.76, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "international cooperation frameworks.", "start": 163.92, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "From this perspective, Egypt as a", "start": 166.64, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "founding member of the United Nations", "start": 168.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "believes that restoring trust requires", "start": 170.959, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "three interconnected pillars. Justice in", "start": 173.44, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "representation and decision making,", "start": 176.319, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "justice in the application of the law,", "start": 178.56, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "and justice in the distribution of", "start": 180.72, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "development and transformation", "start": 182.64, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "opportunities. This is not a call to", "start": 184.56, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "rebuild the international system from", "start": 187.04, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "scratch. It is a call to fulfill its", "start": 189.12, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "original promises and purposes, notably", "start": 191.519, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "sovereign equality among states, respect", "start": 194.4, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "for law, peaceful settlement of", "start": 196.8, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "disputes, international cooperation for", "start": 198.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "the benefit of peoples, and enabling", "start": 201.36, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "them to reap the benefits of", "start": 203.68, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "accelerating scientific progress. The", "start": 205.36, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "multilateral international system", "start": 208.319, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "remains an indispensable choice.", "start": 210.239, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "However, its survival depends on", "start": 213.2, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "strengthening justice and ensuring the", "start": 215.599, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "effectiveness and sustainability of its", "start": 217.76, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "institutions instead of merely repeating", "start": 219.84, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "the principles for which it was", "start": 222.4, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "established without making meaningful", "start": 224.159, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "action. Mr. President, if justice in the", "start": 226.879, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "application of rules is the litmus test", "start": 229.92, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "of the credibility of the international", "start": 232.319, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "system, then the Palestinian issue", "start": 234.319, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "remains the clearest example of the", "start": 236.959, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "existing dysfunction. What the", "start": 239.28, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Palestinian people have endured and", "start": 241.519, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "continue to endure in terms of", "start": 244.0, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "suffering, repression and violations", "start": 245.92, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "must not become a normalized reality or", "start": 248.319, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "a protracted crisis managed managed from", "start": 251.439, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "one cycle to the other. securing the", "start": 254.799, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "ceasefire and the Gaza Strip in", "start": 257.359, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "accordance with President Trump's and", "start": 259.44, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "the Sharmish summit peace plan, ensuring", "start": 261.359, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "full compliance with it, ending daily", "start": 264.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Israeli violations, completing the the", "start": 267.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "withdrawal, guaranteeing the safe and", "start": 270.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "sustainable delivery of humanitarian", "start": 272.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "aid, enabling the National Committee for", "start": 274.32, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "the Administration of Gaza to carry out", "start": 277.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "its duties, and then moving immediately", "start": 279.28, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "toward early recovery and", "start": 282.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "reconstruction. These are not merely", "start": 283.919, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "humanitarian steps. They are also the", "start": 286.56, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "essential gateway to a serious political", "start": 289.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "process that addresses the root causes", "start": 292.08, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "of the conflict and resolves them. In", "start": 294.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "this context, Egypt reaffirms its", "start": 297.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "categorical rejection of any attempt to", "start": 299.6, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "displace the Palestinian people from", "start": 302.24, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "their land, whether from the Gaza Strip", "start": 304.16, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "or from the West Bank, including East", "start": 306.479, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "Jerusalem. The international community", "start": 308.8, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "as a whole bears a clear responsibility", "start": 311.44, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "to stop systematic Israeli violations of", "start": 313.919, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "international law. Peace cannot be built", "start": 316.8, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "on uprooting a people from their land.", "start": 320.16, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "Believing that stability can be achieved", "start": 324.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "in the region while ignoring the", "start": 326.4, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "suffering of the Palestinian people and", "start": 328.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "merely managing the occupation rather", "start": 331.199, "duration": 8.041}, {"text": "than ending it is nothing but illusion.", "start": 333.6, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "The goal remains unequivocally clear.", "start": 343.6, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "The establishment of an independent,", "start": 346.4, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "sovereign, and territorially contiguous", "start": 348.479, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "Palestinian states state on the lines of", "start": 351.84, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "the 4th of June 1967 with East Jerusalem", "start": 355.039, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "as its capital within the framework of", "start": 358.24, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "the two-state solution and in accordance", "start": 360.56, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "with international legitimacy", "start": 362.72, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "resolutions. This requires preserving", "start": 364.4, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the unity of the Palestinian territory", "start": 366.8, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "and the Palestinian political system,", "start": 368.96, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "enabling the Palestinian people to", "start": 371.36, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "manage their own affairs and build their", "start": 373.12, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "state, and ensuring that the", "start": 375.12, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "international community fulfills its", "start": 376.96, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "responsibility to protect civilians,", "start": 379.039, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "reject collective collective punishment,", "start": 381.12, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "and guarantee respect for international", "start": 383.68, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "humanitarian law. It also requires", "start": 385.919, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "recognizing Palestinian rights as", "start": 388.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "inalienable rights, not as bargaining", "start": 390.16, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "chips, to be granted or withheld.", "start": 392.56, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "According to power balances, political", "start": 394.72, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "posturing or electoral calculations,", "start": 397.36, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Egypt has shouldered its responsibility", "start": 400.319, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "alongside its partners to secure the", "start": 402.88, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "ceasefire. It has been the largest", "start": 405.039, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "provider of humanitarian assistance", "start": 408.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "reaching the Gaza Strip.", "start": 410.08, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Egypt will continue to work toward", "start": 412.96, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "reconstruction and opening a viable", "start": 415.28, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "political horizon.", "start": 417.84, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "However, the success of these efforts", "start": 420.0, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "hinges on an international will capable", "start": 422.4, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "of transforming legitimacy into decisive", "start": 425.12, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "international action that moves from", "start": 428.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "managing the tra the tragedy to ending", "start": 430.8, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "its causes. Mr. President, the", "start": 433.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "experience of our region confirms that", "start": 436.0, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "managing crisis rather than resolving", "start": 438.16, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "them does not create stability. Rather,", "start": 440.4, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "it postpones the explosion and increases", "start": 442.96, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "its costs. Accordingly, Egypt Egypt", "start": 445.919, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "remains committed to a clear vision for", "start": 448.72, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "regional security based on state", "start": 451.12, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "sovereignty, territorial integrity,", "start": 453.199, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "respect for national institutions,", "start": 455.36, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "rejection of the dismantling of states", "start": 457.52, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "or the creation of parallel entities and", "start": 459.84, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "prioritizing political solutions and", "start": 462.56, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "inclusive national settlements over the", "start": 465.039, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "logic of force and the imposition of a", "start": 467.52, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "fet accompliant", "start": 470.0, "duration": 3.24}, {"text": "ocean to the Gulf.", "start": 475.12, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Circumstances and details may differ,", "start": 476.639, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "but the capable national state that", "start": 479.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "embraces all its citizens and legitimate", "start": 481.84, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "institutions remain the only true", "start": 484.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "foundation for stability.", "start": 486.72, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Security is indivisible. The security of", "start": 490.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "one state cannot be built upon the", "start": 493.44, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "insecurity of its neighbors or upon", "start": 496.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "threats to shipping, trade, and energy", "start": 498.4, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "roots or violations of state sovereignty", "start": 500.72, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "through attacks carried out in violation", "start": 503.36, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "of international law. Likewise, any", "start": 505.52, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "regional actor that believes that its", "start": 508.319, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "political econom or economic interests", "start": 510.56, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "can be achieve achieved by undermining", "start": 512.959, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "national state institutions, supporting", "start": 515.68, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "militias or promoting separatist agendas", "start": 518.08, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "and civil conflict clearly becomes part", "start": 521.039, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "of the problem.", "start": 524.48, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Confronting such actors and their", "start": 526.56, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "practices becomes the responsibility of", "start": 528.56, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "the international community as a whole.", "start": 530.959, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "Therefore,", "start": 535.36, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "regional crisis cannot be treated as", "start": 537.279, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "isolated cases. They must be viewed", "start": 540.72, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "within an interconnected regional", "start": 543.76, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "security environment that supports the", "start": 546.32, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "state's institutions, unity, and", "start": 549.36, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "sovereignty that encourages political", "start": 551.839, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "settlements and peace building based on", "start": 554.72, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "the principle of national and regional", "start": 557.92, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "ownership of solutions.", "start": 560.08, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "ending external interferences and", "start": 562.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "preventing crises from turning into", "start": 565.04, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "arenas for regional and international", "start": 567.12, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "competition over the resources and", "start": 569.36, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "capabilities of the peoples of the", "start": 571.92, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "region. The protection of states and", "start": 573.839, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "their sovereignty is inseparable from", "start": 575.92, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "pro protecting the resources upon which", "start": 577.839, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "people's livelihoods depend. In this", "start": 580.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "context, I wish to state clearly and", "start": 582.8, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "unequ unequivoc unequivocally that", "start": 585.04, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "Egypt's water security is an existential", "start": 588.48, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "issue that is not open to compromise.", "start": 591.279, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "The Nile is not merely an economic", "start": 594.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "resource. It is the lifeline upon which", "start": 596.16, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "the existence and development of", "start": 598.72, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Egyptian society have depended", "start": 600.64, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "throughout history. Egypt believes that", "start": 602.8, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "trans trans boundary water resources", "start": 605.839, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "should be a field for cooperation and", "start": 608.48, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "integration not conflict. We also", "start": 610.64, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "believe that water security and", "start": 612.88, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "development are not contradictory", "start": 614.48, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "objectives but complimentary ones when", "start": 616.64, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "political will exists when intentions", "start": 619.519, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "are sincere and when international law", "start": 622.079, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "is respected.", "start": 624.72, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "We do not oppose the right of any people", "start": 626.64, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "to development rather we defend a clear", "start": 628.959, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "and just principle that the development", "start": 632.079, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "of one party must not be built upon", "start": 634.88, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "causing harm to others. Shared resources", "start": 637.76, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "cannot be managed through unilateral", "start": 640.72, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "measures or feta policies. They must be", "start": 643.12, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "managed through cooperation, good", "start": 646.8, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "neighborliness, and the conclusion of", "start": 648.72, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "binding agreements in accordance with", "start": 650.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "international law that preserve the", "start": 653.2, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "legitimate rights and interests of all", "start": 655.44, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "parties. In this regard, Egypt preserves", "start": 657.76, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "reserves its legitimate and", "start": 660.72, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "internationally recognized right under", "start": 662.48, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "the under the charter of the United", "start": 664.56, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Nations and international law to protect", "start": 666.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "its water security and preserve the", "start": 668.64, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "existential resources of its people.", "start": 670.8, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "Amid the multiple threats facing our", "start": 675.519, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "region,", "start": 677.6, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "we call the crisis of brotherly Sudan. A", "start": 679.6, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "crisis whose consequences extend beyond", "start": 682.64, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "military confrontations to affect the", "start": 685.6, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "security and safety of civilians and", "start": 687.92, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "threaten to dismantle the state", "start": 690.399, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "institutions. In confronting these", "start": 692.64, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "threats and dangers, the Sudan has in", "start": 695.519, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "Egypt a strong supporter of its people", "start": 698.32, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "and their right to unity", "start": 700.88, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "to institutions capable of safeguarding", "start": 703.44, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "their resources and to a justice that", "start": 705.76, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "upholds their dignity. Mr. President,", "start": 708.399, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "justice in rules is not complete if the", "start": 711.6, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "institutions that make decisions", "start": 714.64, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "do not fairly represent the world they", "start": 718.24, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "govern.", "start": 721.04, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "More than eight decades have passed", "start": 725.279, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "since the founding of the United", "start": 727.6, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Nations. Yet the structure of the", "start": 729.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "international systems institutions,", "start": 731.92, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "particularly the security council, still", "start": 734.0, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "reflect historical balances that have", "start": 736.399, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "become outdated. Institutions that were", "start": 739.12, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "created for a different word cannot", "start": 742.16, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "maintain full legitimacy and", "start": 744.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "effectiveness if they do not reflect the", "start": 746.48, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "word they are meant to serve today and", "start": 749.2, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "represent the concerns and interests of", "start": 752.16, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "the majority of its population. In this", "start": 754.639, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "context, Egypt continues to advocate", "start": 757.68, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "genuine and comprehensive reform of the", "start": 760.079, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "security council in accordance with the", "start": 762.32, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "esolini consensus and the cert", "start": 764.88, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "declaration, particularly to mend the", "start": 766.88, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "historical injustice suffered by Africa.", "start": 769.519, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "The imbalance in political", "start": 773.2, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "representation is matched by another", "start": 774.8, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "imbalance in the global economy.", "start": 777.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Developing countries are required to", "start": 779.839, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "accelerate development, create jobs,", "start": 782.0, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "finance green transitions, and adapt to", "start": 784.48, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "crisis while simultaneously facing", "start": 787.519, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "growing debt burdens, higher financing", "start": 790.32, "duration": 6.959}, {"text": "costs, and a shrinking fiscal space.", "start": 793.6, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "Therefore, reforming international", "start": 797.279, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "financial architecture is no longer a", "start": 799.279, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "luxury, but a necessity. We need", "start": 802.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "financial institutions that are more", "start": 804.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "representative and responsive. We need", "start": 806.56, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "expanded concessional financing, greater", "start": 808.88, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "mobilization and lending capacities for", "start": 811.76, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "multilateral development banks and", "start": 814.639, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "accelerated debt work out in a fair and", "start": 817.04, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "effective manner. We need innovative", "start": 820.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "financing tools", "start": 822.88, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "and a fairer system for assessing", "start": 825.44, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "country's needs and investment risks.", "start": 828.56, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "thus enabling the mobilization of", "start": 832.16, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "private capital without shifting risks", "start": 834.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "onto the most vulnerable countries.", "start": 837.04, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Countries should not be forced to choose", "start": 840.0, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "between debt servicing and financing", "start": 841.92, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "education, health care, food security", "start": 844.639, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "and essential infrastructure.", "start": 846.88, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "Development is not charity. It is a", "start": 848.88, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "right and a shared interest. Investing", "start": 851.199, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "in development is an investment in", "start": 853.68, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "global stability and in the ability of", "start": 855.839, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "states to prevent crisis before they", "start": 858.32, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "become crossber humanitarian and", "start": 861.04, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "security crisis. Mr. President,", "start": 863.6, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "as we work to correct the imbalances", "start": 867.76, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "inherited from the last century, we must", "start": 870.079, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "not allow them to be reproduced in the", "start": 873.199, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "future.", "start": 876.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Artificial intelligence opens boundless", "start": 879.199, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "horizons for growth, knowledge,", "start": 881.6, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "innovation, and improved services. Yet,", "start": 883.839, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "it may also create a vast new divide in", "start": 886.8, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "power linked to computing capacity, data", "start": 889.68, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "models, skills, and financing.", "start": 893.68, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "Therefore, managing this transformation", "start": 897.199, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "requires the establishment of governance", "start": 900.32, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "frameworks for artificial intelligence", "start": 903.279, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "and emerging technologies on the basis", "start": 905.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "that technology is a global public", "start": 908.0, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "benefit and not an exclusive privilege", "start": 910.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "enjoyed by a limited number of states or", "start": 912.88, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "corporations. Egypt supports the role of", "start": 915.36, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "the United Nations and a global dialogue", "start": 918.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "to develop principles that balance", "start": 921.279, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "innovation and responsibility, protect", "start": 923.68, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "privacy, guarantee transparency,", "start": 926.16, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "accountability, non-discrimination,", "start": 928.399, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "human oversight, respect for", "start": 930.72, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "international law, technology and", "start": 932.639, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "knowledge transfer,", "start": 935.199, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "financing of digital infrastructure and", "start": 937.76, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "skills development.", "start": 941.279, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "This would enable developing countries", "start": 943.36, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "to become producers and developers of", "start": 945.279, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "technology rather than merely being", "start": 947.68, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "markets for its consumption. Artificial", "start": 949.92, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "intelligence should also reflect the", "start": 952.639, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "linguistic and cultural diversity of the", "start": 954.48, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "word.", "start": 956.88, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "Arab and African languages and", "start": 958.72, "duration": 3.679}, {"text": "communities should receive fair", "start": 960.48, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "representation in data and models. Egypt", "start": 962.399, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "has launched the second edition of its", "start": 965.839, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "national artificial intelligence", "start": 968.079, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "strategy 2025 2030 grounded in its firm", "start": 970.079, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "conviction that the safe and responsible", "start": 975.04, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "use of technology and the development of", "start": 977.519, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "national capacities are inseparable", "start": 980.16, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "requirements.", "start": 982.56, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "The same principle governs the green", "start": 984.079, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "transition. There can be no just", "start": 986.24, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "transition if ambition is dissociated", "start": 988.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "from fair implementation. Climate action", "start": 990.72, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "must go hand inhand with development,", "start": 993.68, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "poverty reduction and job creation.", "start": 995.839, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "Adaptation, water security, and food", "start": 999.6, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "security must receive the priority they", "start": 1002.24, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "deserve, especially in Africa and the", "start": 1005.04, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "countries most vulnerable to the impacts", "start": 1007.6, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "of climate change.", "start": 1009.839, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "Drawing on Egypt's experience in hosting", "start": 1012.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "the climate conference in Shermish and", "start": 1014.56, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "the decision it adopted, we can affirm", "start": 1017.04, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "that the gap no longer lies in", "start": 1019.839, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "diagnosing the problem, but in", "start": 1022.32, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "implementation, especially in", "start": 1024.319, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "translating commitments into financing", "start": 1026.48, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "flows, projects and technologies that", "start": 1028.72, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "reach the countries and communities most", "start": 1031.439, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "in need. In a world where geopolitical", "start": 1033.919, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "and technological transformations are", "start": 1036.959, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "accelerating, this must not lead us into", "start": 1039.36, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "more dangerous arms races.", "start": 1042.88, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Therefore, Egypt reaffirms its", "start": 1046.48, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "commitment to a balanced system of", "start": 1048.4, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "disarmament and non-prololiferation", "start": 1050.4, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "free from double standards", "start": 1053.2, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "and its commitment to the goal of", "start": 1055.919, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "establishing a Middle East free of", "start": 1057.919, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "nuclear weapons and all other weapons of", "start": 1060.48, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "mass destruction.", "start": 1063.36, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "Collective security is not achieved", "start": 1065.12, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "through the accumulation of instruments", "start": 1067.12, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "of destruction. Rather, it is achieved", "start": 1069.039, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "through equal rules, obligations", "start": 1071.2, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "applicable to all and a political will", "start": 1073.44, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "that prioritizes the prevention of", "start": 1075.919, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "escalation rather than having a delayed", "start": 1077.919, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "reaction after crisis occur. Mr.", "start": 1080.32, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "President, as Egypt presents this", "start": 1083.52, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "vision, it is not merely calling for a", "start": 1085.679, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "reform of the international system.", "start": 1087.919, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "Egypt is putting its experience and", "start": 1090.24, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "capabilities in service of solutions", "start": 1092.24, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "drawing upon its Arab, African and", "start": 1095.039, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "Meditar Mediterranean heritage, its", "start": 1097.44, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "historic role in founding the", "start": 1100.4, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "multilateral international order and its", "start": 1102.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "principled commitment to its survival", "start": 1104.64, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "and sustainability. Egypt will remain a", "start": 1106.96, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "bridge for cooperation and a partner to", "start": 1109.919, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "all those who seek a more just and", "start": 1112.4, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "effective international system. We will", "start": 1114.559, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "continue investing in partnerships with", "start": 1117.2, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "all parties. We remain open to", "start": 1119.2, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "cooperation and exchange of expertise", "start": 1121.44, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "and working with all nations in both the", "start": 1123.6, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "global north and the global south on", "start": 1126.24, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "solutions that do not impose a single", "start": 1128.559, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "model but respect national priorities", "start": 1130.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "and are based on shared ownership.", "start": 1133.039, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Legitimacy gains meaning when it", "start": 1135.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "produces results. Institutions regain", "start": 1137.679, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "trust when they do justice to those they", "start": 1140.24, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "serve. Trust is not demanded. It is", "start": 1142.64, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "built through justice. Transformation is", "start": 1145.36, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "not imposed. It is managed through", "start": 1148.08, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "participation. Egypt will continue to", "start": 1150.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "support every effort that restores trust", "start": 1152.48, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "and effectiveness to our multilateral", "start": 1154.72, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "international system and contributes to", "start": 1156.799, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "managing the transformations of our", "start": 1159.28, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "rapidly changing word in a fair and", "start": 1161.36, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "participatory manner serving the", "start": 1163.919, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "interests of our peoples and future", "start": 1166.08, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "generations.", "start": 1168.32, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "Before concluding, I wish to take this", "start": 1169.84, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "opportunity from this rostrm to extend", "start": 1172.48, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "our sincere thanks and appreciation to", "start": 1175.36, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Mr. Antonio Guterish, Secretary General", "start": 1178.0, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "of the United Nations, who has led the", "start": 1180.88, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "organization through one of the most", "start": 1183.84, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "difficult and critical periods in its", "start": 1186.24, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "history with courage, integrity,", "start": 1188.4, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "and in a sincere commitment to", "start": 1191.919, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "fulfilling his mandate to protect", "start": 1194.08, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "international law, preserve the standing", "start": 1196.08, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "and role of the United Nations, maintain", "start": 1198.64, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "its credibility and moral authority, and", "start": 1201.12, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "defend the principles upon which the", "start": 1204.4, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "organization was founded.", "start": 1206.799, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "These efforts will remain appreciated", "start": 1208.799, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "and remembered as I express our profound", "start": 1210.96, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "gratitude for all that he has done. I", "start": 1214.16, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "wish him every success in his future", "start": 1217.28, "duration": 8.44}, {"text": "endeavors. Thank you for your attention.", "start": 1220.559, "duration": 5.161}, {"text": "On behalf of the general assembly,", "start": 1233.2, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "I thank his excellency the prime", "start": 1236.08, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "minister of Egypt.", "start": 1238.32, "duration": 3.28}]